# Quick Revision

```text
STACK
│
├── Per thread
├── Method calls
├── Stack frames
├── Local execution data
└── Recursion can exhaust it


HEAP
│
├── Shared between threads
├── Objects
├── Arrays
├── Objects can survive method return
└── Garbage Collector manages unreachable objects
```

## One thing I don't want to forget

> **A reference is not the object itself.**

For:

```java
Student s = new Student();
```

think:

```text
s ─────────→ Student object
reference      object
```

Understanding this makes a lot of other Java concepts easier:

**OOP → references → objects → collections → garbage collection → multithreading.**
